Enhancement: Harden backups of changing files and large file counts

Restic now compares a regular file's size and modification time immediately
before and after reading it. If the file changes or disappears during the read,
the mismatch is reported and recorded in a change journal. Pending records are
associated with the next successful snapshot; the journal location can be
overridden with `--change-journal`.

Backups with many small files can use `--max-open-files` to bound the number of
open file handles. Additional files wait for a free slot instead of failing with
"too many open files". The read buffer/block size is configurable with
`--read-block-size`; file read concurrency remains configurable with
`--read-concurrency`.

Permission and disappearance errors continue to be reported while allowing the
remaining backup to proceed. Cancellation prevents new work from being queued
and waits for active workers to finish; completed packs are stored atomically
and are not truncated by cancellation.

